### 3. Subsystem Breakdown

#### 3.1 Networking & Wire Protocol (`core/networking/`)
- [`message_frame.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/networking/message_frame.hpp): Implements custom binary framing with magic bytes `0x44494350` (`"DICP"`), 16-bit protocol version, 16-bit message type, 32-bit payload length, and MTU enforcement ($\le 1200$ bytes to prevent IP fragmentation).
- [`udp_transport.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/networking/udp_transport.hpp): Boost.Asio non-blocking asynchronous UDP socket transport for probes and gossip dissemination.
- [`tcp_transport.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/networking/tcp_transport.hpp): Length-prefixed framed TCP transport for anti-entropy bulk state synchronization (`MSG_SYNC_REQUEST` / `MSG_SYNC_RESPONSE`).

#### 3.2 Membership & SWIM Failure Detection (`core/membership/`, `core/gossip/`)
- [`node_identity.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/agent/node_identity.hpp): Tracks stable `node_id`, volatile `boot_id` (UUIDv4), network ports, and an atomic `incarnation` counter.
- [`membership_manager.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/membership/membership_manager.hpp): Implements the deterministic state machine:
  1. **Higher incarnation wins unconditionally.**
  2. **Equal incarnation deterministic precedence:** $\text{DEAD} > \text{SUSPECT} > \text{ALIVE}$.
  3. `NODE_LEFT` (graceful departure) is an absorbing final state.
- [`failure_detector.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/membership/failure_detector.hpp):
  - Sends direct `MSG_PING` to random peers.
  - If a probe times out, initiates indirect `MSG_PING_REQ` to $k$ random intermediaries to probe the target on its behalf.
  - If indirect probes also fail, marks the target as `SUSPECT` and arms a suspicion timer.
  - **Refutation mechanism:** If a node receives a rumor that it is `SUSPECT` or `DEAD`, it increments its incarnation number ($I_{new} = I_{old} + 1$) and broadcasts an `ALIVE` refutation.
  - If no refutation arrives before the timer expires, the node transitions to `DEAD`.
- [`gossip_engine.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/gossip/gossip_engine.hpp) & [`dissemination_queue.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/gossip/dissemination_queue.hpp): Bounded priority queue with fanout tracking ($f = 3$) and an LRU deduplication cache (5000 entries) to avoid broadcast storms.

#### 3.3 Replicated Service Registry (`core/registry/`)
- [`service_registry.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/registry/service_registry.hpp):
  - Manages registered service instances, addresses, ports, weights, and health status.
  - **Lease TTL:** Services hold time-to-live leases (default 10s) and must renew heartbeats.
  - **Tombstones:** Expired/deregistered services are soft-deleted as tombstones (retained for 60s) to prevent out-of-order gossip resurrection before being safely purged.

#### 3.4 Active Health Monitoring (`core/health/`)
- [`health_monitor.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/health/health_monitor.hpp):
  - Decouples physical node health from individual service health (a node can be `ALIVE` while a container running on it is dead).
  - Uses Boost.Beast asynchronous HTTP client to poll service `/health` endpoints.
  - **Hysteresis filtering:** Requires $N$ consecutive failures to mark `UNHEALTHY`, and $M$ consecutive successes to restore `HEALTHY`, preventing flapping.

#### 3.5 Asynchronous Data Plane & HTTP Reverse Proxy (`core/load_balancer/`)
- [`backend_snapshot.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/load_balancer/backend_snapshot.hpp): Versioned, immutable backend snapshots.
- [`load_balancer_strategy.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/load_balancer/load_balancer_strategy.hpp): 4 load balancing algorithms:
  1. **Round Robin**: Atomic counter cycling across eligible instances.
  2. **Weighted Round Robin**: Smooth deficit distribution honoring configured instance weights.
  3. **Least Connections**: Selects the instance with the lowest active in-flight TCP connections (`active_connections.load()`).
  4. **Consistent Hashing**: 100 virtual nodes per endpoint on an FNV-1a ring with sticky routing per `X-Routing-Key`.
- [`http_proxy.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/load_balancer/http_proxy.hpp):
  - **Lock-free hot path:** Reads snapshots via `std::atomic_load(&snapshot_)`. In-flight requests safely reference the existing snapshot, while new requests immediately use updated snapshots swapped via `std::atomic_store`.
  - Admin endpoints: `/admin/backends`, `POST /admin/snapshot` (hot snapshot ingestion), `POST /admin/strategy` (dynamic strategy switching), and `/metrics`.

#### 3.6 Distributed Configuration & Persistence (`core/config_manager/`, `core/storage/`)
- [`config_manager.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/config_manager/config_manager.hpp): Hierarchical scopes (`GLOBAL`, `DATACENTER`, `NODE`, `SERVICE`) with monotonic 64-bit version conflict resolution and auditable forward rollback.
- [`sqlite_storage.hpp`](file:///home/pbyanshu/Downloads/CN%20PORJECT/core/storage/sqlite_storage.hpp): Embedded SQLite database with `PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL` and prepared statements. Persists node records so restarting nodes automatically recover and increment their incarnation counter.

#### 3.7 Python Management API (`management/`)
